{"t": 1794112098.541584, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "## Problem\n\n`catalog.pager.page(items, 1, size)` returns the second page, but the API documents page numbers as 1-based (`?page=1` is the first page). See #57.\n\n## Fix\n\nCompute the slice offset as `(number - 1) * size` instead of `number * size`.\n\n## Verification\n\n```python\n>>> page(list(range(10)), 1, 3)\n[0, 1, 2]\n>>> page(list(range(10)), 2, 3)\n[3, 4, 5]\n```\n\nFixes #57", "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "fix(pager): treat page numbers as 1-based"}, "ok": true}
